{
  "vcon": "0.4.0",
  "uuid": "4390863e-425d-8b25-91e2-b5c33f244956",
  "created_at": "2026-01-14T11:45:42-05:00",
  "subject": "Inbound call, Public Works",
  "parties": [
    {
      "name": "Mike Reardon",
      "role": "resident",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    },
    {
      "name": "Denise Arruda",
      "role": "clerk",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    }
  ],
  "dialog": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-14T11:41:57-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Public Works, this is Denise."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-14T11:42:00-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Hi, yes, hi. Can you hear me okay? I'm on my cell and it's not great where I am."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-14T11:42:09-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I can hear you fine. Go ahead."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-14T11:42:13-05:00",
      "duration": 23,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. I have a question about recycling. What's allowed now? Like what can actually go in the bin. I want to make sure I'm doing it right, because I don't want to get a tag or whatever, you know, I just want to do it right. Is that okay to ask?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-14T11:42:36-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Absolutely, that's what we're here for. What are you trying to put in?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-14T11:42:43-05:00",
      "duration": 19,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "So, pizza boxes. Can the pizza box go in? Because there's grease on it. And glass, jars and bottles, is glass still okay? And then those plastic clamshell things, the ones the berries and the salad come in. [line breaks up] ...those okay?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-14T11:43:02-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "You broke up on the last part. Clamshells, you said?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-14T11:43:07-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yeah, the clamshells. The clear plastic ones with the hinge."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-14T11:43:12-05:00",
      "duration": 29,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. In general, a pizza box that's clean cardboard is fine, but the greasy part, the soiled bottom, usually belongs in the trash. You can tear off the clean lid and recycle that. Glass bottles and jars are generally accepted, just empty and rinsed, lids off. Clamshells I'm less sure of, because it depends on the plastic type and what the processor is taking right now."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-14T11:43:41-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "So the clamshells, are they okay or not okay? I don't want to put them in if they're not okay."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-14T11:43:50-05:00",
      "duration": 12,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I can't say yes for certain on those. If you're unsure, keep them out of the bin for now. A bad item can spoil a whole load."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-14T11:44:02-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Right, right. So leave them out. And the pizza box, just the top part, the clean part. That's okay?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-14T11:44:11-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes, the clean part is fine. Greasy part goes in the trash."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-14T11:44:17-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. Okay, good. And the glass, rinsed, no lids. That's okay?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-14T11:44:23-05:00",
      "duration": 2,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "That's right."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-14T11:44:25-05:00",
      "duration": 17,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Alright. Um, one more thing. Can I get a supervisor to call me back? Just so somebody there can confirm the whole list for me, especially the plastic ones. I'd feel better with it from a supervisor."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-14T11:44:42-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Sure, I can put in a message for a supervisor. What's a good number?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-14T11:44:49-05:00",
      "duration": 2,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "It's 401-555-0160."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-14T11:44:51-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Zero-one-six-zero, got it. And it's Mike?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-14T11:44:55-05:00",
      "duration": 2,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Mike Reardon. R-E-A-R-D-O-N."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-14T11:44:57-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Thanks, Mike. I'll note it's about the recycling list, mainly the clamshells. They'll call you back, probably today or tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-14T11:45:06-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, that's okay. Tomorrow is fine. Sorry, you probably hear this all day, people asking what goes in the bin."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-14T11:45:15-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "It's a common one, don't worry about it."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-14T11:45:19-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. So just to be sure, the supervisor will call, and until then I leave the clamshells out. That's okay?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-14T11:45:28-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "That's right. Message is going in now."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-14T11:45:32-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Great. Thank you. Thanks for your help."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-14T11:45:36-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "You're welcome, Mike. Have a good afternoon."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-14T11:45:40-05:00",
      "duration": 2,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "You too. Bye."
    }
  ],
